nearly down, catching me off guard.

205
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:06,366
His taste is completely
traditional, though.

206
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:08,160
- Old man palate. - Exactly.

207
00:08:08,930 --> 00:08:10,030
Sounds good.

208
00:08:10,090 --> 00:08:11,900
I am curious about Tsuki's Table too.

209
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,430
- May I show you? - Tsuki's Table.

210
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:18,340
I hope you can figure it
out. Yes. Tsuki's Table.

211
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,400
Tsuki's Table.

212
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:21,990
- Still, it is better than mine.
- It is better than mine.

213
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:24,740
- I will explain this one. - Sounds good.

214
00:08:24,810 --> 00:08:28,510
This is the food that got me
through my days as a Trainee.

215
00:08:28,650 --> 00:08:30,510
- Sausage and Vegetable Stir-fry.
- Sausages?

216
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:32,780
Look closely. It really
looks just like this.

217
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:33,920
Rose Tteokbokki.

218
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,949
- Intestines. Stir-fried Intestines.
- Intestines.

219
00:08:35,950 --> 00:08:37,430
- Stir-fried Intestines. - Motsunabe?

220
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,590
I do not know what that
is. This is Braised Kimchi.

221
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,690
- What? - Braised Kimchi.

222
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:42,760
- What? - Braised Kimchi?

223
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:45,730
- Braised Kimchi is...
- It is obviously Braised Kimchi.

224
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,980
Why does it look like that?

225
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:48,230
- BamBam. - I mean...

226
00:08:48,231 --> 00:08:50,746
No, no, not the drawing, but why
does Braised Kimchi look like that?

227
00:08:50,770 --> 00:08:53,000
- Why does it look like that?
- No. Watch carefully.

228
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,470
I added things I like.

229
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:59,310
Here's pork belly, and here's some ham.

230
00:08:59,610 --> 00:09:01,410
This yellow part is soft tofu.

231
00:09:01,550 --> 00:09:02,786
- Soft tofu.
- Oh, there was yellow in there.

232
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:03,810
This is kimchi.

233
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,320
- Now I see it.
- Too many toppings to tell.

234
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:09,196
- Who puts that many toppings...
- You see it now, right?

235
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:10,490
When I was a trainee,

236
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:13,260
my first Korean delivery
was Braised Kimchi.

237
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:16,790
It was so spicy and flavorful, a
comfort food full of memories,

238
00:09:17,630 --> 00:09:18,630
Braised Kimchi.

239
00:09:18,631 --> 00:09:23,100
Back then, eating
spicy food felt really cool.

240
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,716
Though it was super
spicy, I pretended it wasn't...

241
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:25,860
and kept eating like this...

242
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:28,010
Crying and tearing up.

243
00:09:28,210 --> 00:09:30,130
I had a low spice
tolerance, but to build it up,

244
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:32,110
I kept eating it.

245
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:34,210
All right, next up is Jaemin.

246
00:09:34,410 --> 00:09:37,250
I'm really looking forward
to this. Nice drawing.

247
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:38,720
Nice drawing.

248
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:40,850
