1023
00:39:35,180 --> 00:39:36,950
You can't really tell
just by looking at it,

1024
00:39:37,010 --> 00:39:38,010
Right.

1025
00:39:38,380 --> 00:39:42,080
But what do you think is the
kick in Jaemin's Braised Kimchi?

1026
00:39:42,150 --> 00:39:43,190
What's the kick here?

1027
00:39:43,690 --> 00:39:46,190
My kick is actually perilla seed powder.

1028
00:39:46,260 --> 00:39:48,266
(The Braised Kimchi's
Kick is perilla seed powder.)

1029
00:39:48,290 --> 00:39:50,129
No wonder.

1030
00:39:50,130 --> 00:39:51,370
(Plenty of perilla seed powder)

1031
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:53,360
- I had no idea. - Perilla seed powder?

1032
00:39:53,430 --> 00:39:57,070
- That explains the scent...
- The aroma and the flavor...

1033
00:39:57,130 --> 00:39:58,476
blends right into the perilla leaves,

1034
00:39:58,500 --> 00:40:00,180
so it feels like a subtle touch of makeup.

1035
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:03,670
And it makes the Braised
Kimchi taste so refined.

1036
00:40:03,970 --> 00:40:05,110
Exactly.

1037
00:40:05,780 --> 00:40:08,509
So rather than mixing the
seasoned perilla leaves in,

1038
00:40:08,510 --> 00:40:09,749
because if you mix it,

1039
00:40:09,750 --> 00:40:11,356
- the perilla powder...
- Right, it just scatters.

1040
00:40:11,380 --> 00:40:13,450
Yes, it gets all
scattered, so topping it...

1041
00:40:13,520 --> 00:40:16,720
and eating it like this is the key Kick.

1042
00:40:17,990 --> 00:40:20,190
- You're a genius. - It's so delicious.

1043
00:40:21,390 --> 00:40:22,706
Let's try Stir-fried Tomato
and Egg on its own,

1044
00:40:22,730 --> 00:40:24,210
and then wrapped with seaweed crisps.

1045
00:40:25,460 --> 00:40:28,229
(Eating it as is without seaweed crisps)

1046
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:29,700
(How is it?)

1047
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:33,900
Try it. Hurry up and try it.

1048
00:40:34,900 --> 00:40:40,480
(Tsuki tries it with seaweed crisps.)

1049
00:40:40,780 --> 00:40:42,510
(Incomprehensible)

1050
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:44,780
(Carmen takes a bite.)

1051
00:40:45,350 --> 00:40:47,619
How can Stir-fried Tomato and
Egg go so well with seaweed?

1052
00:40:47,620 --> 00:40:48,879
They go together so well.

1053
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:51,120
- It's so good. - It's so savory.

1054
00:40:52,050 --> 00:40:55,290
The whole world needs to
know about this. It's so good.

1055
00:40:56,060 --> 00:40:58,989
Eating it with seaweed
crisps is definitely delicious.

1056
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:00,700
- Right? Good, isn't it? - It's so good.

1057
00:41:00,860 --> 00:41:02,570
(Devouring IT)

1058
00:41:02,630 --> 00:41:03,630
Perfect with rice.

1059
00:41:03,970 --> 00:41:08,369
(He might eat the bowl too.)

1060
00:41:08,370 --> 00:41:12,580
(You can tell it's delicious
just by looking at Lele.)

1061
00:41:12,810 --> 00:41:14,440
- But these two... - Yes?

1062
00:41:14,880 --> 00:41:16,156
They go surprisingly well together.

1063
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:17,309
The two go well together.

1064
00:41:17,310 --> 00:41:19,350
- In a unique way. - Exactly.

1065
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:21,850
It's totally, totally meant for rice.

1066
00:41:22,250 --> 00:41:24,296
The problem right now is
they gave us too little rice.

1067
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:26,389
- True. Way too little.
- Seriously, the rice...

1068
00:41:26,390 --> 00:41:27,519
- Right. - They should have given...

1069
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:29,390
- a bigger portion. - It's not enough.

1070
00:41:29,660 --> 00:41:30,736
I want to mix the rice with this.

1071
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:31,760
It is so good.

1072
00:41:32,160 --> 00:41:34,530
You know we have the
Sauce Pantry over there, right?

1073
00:41:34,600 --> 00:41:35,600
Yes.

1074
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:37,700
- They have all kinds of sauces.
- That's true.

1075
00:41:37,770 --> 00:41:39,930
From there, you can choose
sauces to match your taste.

1076
00:41:40,170 --> 00:41:41,500
Got it.

1077
00:41:41,700 --> 00:41:43,740
Should we go grab some?
Yes, let's go check it out.

1078
00:41:43,970 --> 00:41:46,410
- I'm curious.
- They must have mayonnaise, right?

1079
00:41:47,710 --> 00:41:49,410
I'll go look later. I'm curious.

1080
00:41:49,710 --> 00:41:50,950
But I'll eat first.

1081
00:41:51,180 --> 00:41:54,150
It's open. Exactly. According to our taste.

1082
00:41:54,650 --> 00:41:57,250
(Let's see...)

1083
00:41:58,050 --> 00:41:59,260
There's mayonnaise too.

1084
00:41:59,560 --> 00:42:01,200
Is there anything that goes well with it?

1085
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:03,560
This mayonnaise.

1086
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:05,730
What do we have here?

1087
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:08,640
There are so many interesting things.

1088
00:42:08,900 --> 00:42:10,369
(Finally, he picks one.)

1089
00:42:10,370 --> 00:42:11,370
Is that hot sauce?

1090
00:42:11,371 --> 00:42:12,500
(Finally, he picks one.)

1091
00:42:13,300 --> 00:42:15,700
Satay sauce? I'll give it a try.

1092
00:42:17,070 --> 00:42:18,470
What did you bring?

1093
00:42:18,670 --> 00:42:22,080
- I brought some hot sauce. - Hot sauce?

1094
00:42:22,180 --> 00:42:25,110
I think adding hot sauce to it is good.

1095
00:42:25,810 --> 00:42:27,450
Really? Now I'm curious.

1096
00:42:27,750 --> 00:42:31,020
Actually, when I make Stir-fried
Tomato and Egg at home,

1097
00:42:31,750 --> 00:42:33,390
I sometimes add a bit of hot sauce to it.

1098
00:42:33,660 --> 00:42:36,090
- Do you put that much?
- I like to put a lot.

1099
00:42:36,160 --> 00:42:37,236
I'll put just a moderate amount here.

1100
00:42:37,260 --> 00:42:38,560
Okay. Thank you.

1101
00:42:38,860 --> 00:42:41,260
